393	   pass — these three rules retarget the pattern itself, wherever it appears,
394	   for light mode only. Dark mode does not match any of these selectors and is
395	   completely unaffected.
396	
397	   The attribute selector matches the literal characters Tailwind puts in the
398	   `class` DOM attribute, which is unescaped there even though the generated
399	   CSS selector for the same class has to escape the brackets and commas — so
400	   `[class*="rgba(10,22,48"]` finds it without needing to know the exact
401	   opacity any given instance used. */
402	html[data-theme="light"] [class*="rgba(10,22,48"] {
403	  background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.92), rgba(246,249,253,.98)) !important;
404	  border-color: var(--color-rim);
405	}
406	html[data-theme="light"] [class*="rgba(6,14,36"] {
407	  background: rgba(255,255,255,.85) !important;
408	}
